<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  es-theme-xmb-psp - "Scroll Speed: Normal" (default).
  Sets autoScrollSpeed=150ms on the scrolling gamelist descriptions.
  ES's own default cadence (AUTO_SCROLL_SPEED, TextComponent.cpp:9).
  Selected via UI Settings > Theme Configuration > Scroll Speed > Normal.

  The value is milliseconds between one-pixel steps, NOT a rate - larger is
  slower. It is read only by the vertical scroll path
  (TextComponent.cpp:471,487); the horizontal marquee computes its own speed
  from font metrics and ignores this property entirely (:449).

  Targets cardDesc (PSP Card) and listDesc (List + Details) - the only two
  descriptions in the theme. Box Art Grid is deliberately art-first and has no
  description element, so it has no target here; that is a decision, not an
  omission (#38). Setting a property on an element the selected style does not
  define is a silent no-op - which is exactly how this subset stayed dead from
  v0.11 through v0.12, still naming an element that two redesigns had renamed
  out from under it. scripts/tests/test-scroll-speed.sh now fails if any name
  here is absent from every style file.

  Both scrolling styles declare <view name="detailed,gamecarousel">. Do not add
  the grid view name: any parsed file that registers a view makes hasView()
  true for it, which is how an unstyled built-in grid got built for users who
  had pinned that Gamelist View Style (fixed in b5e2063).

  CC-BY-NC-SA 2.0. See CREDITS.md.
-->
<theme>
  <formatVersion>7</formatVersion>
  <view name="detailed,gamecarousel">
    <text name="cardDesc">
      <autoScrollSpeed>150</autoScrollSpeed>
    </text>
    <text name="listDesc">
      <autoScrollSpeed>150</autoScrollSpeed>
    </text>
  </view>
</theme>
